target:    src/Migration/Migrations/ConvertTablesToUtf8mb4.php
gate:      composer test:migration-deadline
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    declares PASS_SECONDS but never reads it
rationale: Keeps the constant and deletes the only read of it, which is the failure mode a grep cannot see: the class still ADVERTISES a ten-second budget and bounds nothing. ConvertTablesToUtf8mb4 is the most expensive migration in the set -- a CONVERT TO CHARACTER SET per table across six tables, performed as ALGORITHM=COPY, blocking writes throughout -- and it shipped with no budget at all, missed by the first draft of this gate because that draft scanned for do/while and this uses foreach.
---
--- a/src/Migration/Migrations/ConvertTablesToUtf8mb4.php
+++ b/src/Migration/Migrations/ConvertTablesToUtf8mb4.php
@@ -251,11 +251,10 @@
         // there is nothing to checkpoint inside it. What the budget buys is that a six-table
         // conversion does not start another rebuild in a request that is already nearly out of
         // time — the pass stops cleanly instead, and pendingTables() re-derives from
         // information_schema on the next one, so the remaining tables are picked up exactly where
         // this left off.
-        $deadline = microtime(true) + self::PASS_SECONDS;
         $first    = true;
 
         foreach ($pending as $table) {
             // Stop before STARTING another rebuild, not after — but never before the FIRST one.
             // A budget that can decline to do any work at all is not a budget, it is a way for a
